Subject: [PATCH] airoha-pon: expose SET_FORCE_GPIO32_EN to PHY modules

The SCU BSP exports SET_FORCE_GPIO32_EN(), and the EN7581 PHY calls it
when switching PON TX power.  The vendor headers omit the prototype,
which becomes a fatal implicit-declaration error with the Linux 6.18
toolchain.

Signed-off-by: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>
---
--- a/bsp/include/global_inc/modules/scu/ecnt_scu.h
+++ b/bsp/include/global_inc/modules/scu/ecnt_scu.h
@@ -229,4 +229,5 @@
 extern void SET_GPIO_SSR(u32 val);
 
 
+extern void SET_FORCE_GPIO32_EN(u32 mask, u32 bits);
 #endif /* ifndef __ECNT_SCU_H__ */
--- a/bsp/include/scu/ecnt_scu.h
+++ b/bsp/include/scu/ecnt_scu.h
@@ -224,4 +224,5 @@
 extern void SET_WAN_CONF(u32 val);
 
 
+extern void SET_FORCE_GPIO32_EN(u32 mask, u32 bits);
 #endif /* ifndef __ECNT_SCU_H__ */
